[{:db/id "32e65719-9423-5445-8fcf-aaf6c05d97d5" :answer/id #uuid "32e65719-9423-5445-8fcf-aaf6c05d97d5" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$A$ and $C$ only" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "80feb855-589a-53c3-bac3-61637b4af9e4" :answer/id #uuid "80feb855-589a-53c3-bac3-61637b4af9e4" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$A$ only" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "643d71ec-95bc-5042-8b51-322a436c9046" :answer/id #uuid "643d71ec-95bc-5042-8b51-322a436c9046" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$B$ and $C$ only" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "ecf14a96-818d-5db6-9c66-a0d3175bb6b4" :answer/id #uuid "ecf14a96-818d-5db6-9c66-a0d3175bb6b4" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$B$ only" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "e967faa4-e8a6-581c-a3cf-38284b6b90c7" :answer/id #uuid "e967faa4-e8a6-581c-a3cf-38284b6b90c7" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$C$ only" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "fffeded8-fcf5-542f-a921-ded34513e23b" :answer-field/id #uuid "fffeded8-fcf5-542f-a921-ded34513e23b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/choices ["32e65719-9423-5445-8fcf-aaf6c05d97d5" "80feb855-589a-53c3-bac3-61637b4af9e4" "643d71ec-95bc-5042-8b51-322a436c9046" "ecf14a96-818d-5db6-9c66-a0d3175bb6b4" "e967faa4-e8a6-581c-a3cf-38284b6b90c7"] :answer-field/correct "32e65719-9423-5445-8fcf-aaf6c05d97d5" :db/ensure :answer-field/validate} {:db/id "0f863f32-c463-5f07-9482-1c6f6e74c019" :question/id #uuid "0f863f32-c463-5f07-9482-1c6f6e74c019" :question/problem "![](images/4c/4c714262b9da22ea9ad859817db86a3aaf0b29ef811246aedc969bc9999c0348.png)\n\nIdentify the points that lie on the line $y=x+3.$" :question/worked-solution "The plotted points correspond to the $xy$-pairs $A(-3,0)$, $B(-1,4)$ and $C(3,6).$\n\nTo check whether a point lies on the line, we substitute the coordinates of the point into the equation and determine whether the resulting statement is true.\n\n- Substituting the point $A(-3,0)$ results in a true statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =x+3 \\\\ (0) & =1(-3)+3 \\\\ 0 & =0\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the point $A$ does lie on the line.\n\n- Substituting the point $B(-1,4)$ results in a false statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =x+3 \\\\ (4) & =1(-1)+3 \\\\ 4 & =2\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the point $B$ does not lie on the line.\n\n- Substituting the point $C(3,6)$ results in true statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =x+3 \\\\ (6) & =1(3)+3 \\\\ 6 & =6\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the point $C$ does lie on the line.\n\nFinally, only points $A$ and $C$ lie on the line." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["fffeded8-fcf5-542f-a921-ded34513e23b"] :db/ensure :question/validate} {:db/id "0944b8cd-a8ad-5881-872d-cc7841b124b3" :answer/id #uuid "0944b8cd-a8ad-5881-872d-cc7841b124b3" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$A$ and $C$ only" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "cb659afb-f587-5d6a-8397-672e2e9f924f" :answer/id #uuid "cb659afb-f587-5d6a-8397-672e2e9f924f" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$A$ only" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "2e04fce8-d81f-5c10-9a2d-ce00e7cc6157" :answer/id #uuid "2e04fce8-d81f-5c10-9a2d-ce00e7cc6157" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$B$ and $C$ only" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "0a037906-7560-5a7f-af3a-df39ea31c7f5" :answer/id #uuid "0a037906-7560-5a7f-af3a-df39ea31c7f5" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$B$ only" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "64c6d466-8db0-5469-a154-b446a630e557" :answer/id #uuid "64c6d466-8db0-5469-a154-b446a630e557" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$C$ only" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "9124fd28-3c96-58aa-a8b1-46f977a63903" :answer-field/id #uuid "9124fd28-3c96-58aa-a8b1-46f977a63903" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/choices ["0944b8cd-a8ad-5881-872d-cc7841b124b3" "cb659afb-f587-5d6a-8397-672e2e9f924f" "2e04fce8-d81f-5c10-9a2d-ce00e7cc6157" "0a037906-7560-5a7f-af3a-df39ea31c7f5" "64c6d466-8db0-5469-a154-b446a630e557"] :answer-field/correct "0944b8cd-a8ad-5881-872d-cc7841b124b3" :db/ensure :answer-field/validate} {:db/id "b0bb51db-df3a-5c24-9053-c8f5081141e9" :question/id #uuid "b0bb51db-df3a-5c24-9053-c8f5081141e9" :question/problem "![](images/1a/1aa0849898f763eedd84d050a7bd7c24bbb10c8f89c81e3f533622252330814e.png)\n\nIdentify the points that lie on the line $y=3x+4.$" :question/worked-solution "The plotted points correspond to the $xy$-pairs $A(-3,-5)$, $B(1,5)$ and $C(2,10).$\n\nTo check whether a point lies on the line, we substitute the coordinates of the point into the equation and determine whether the resulting statement is true.\n\n- Substituting the point $A(-3,-5)$ results in a true statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =3x+4 \\\\ (-5) & =3(-3)+4 \\\\ -5 & =-5\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the point $A$ does lie on the line.\n\n- Substituting the point $B(1,5)$ results in a false statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =3x+4 \\\\ (5) & =3(1)+4 \\\\ 5 & =7\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the point $B$ does not lie on the line.\n\n- Substituting the point $C(2,10)$ results in true statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =3x+4 \\\\ (10) & =3(2)+4 \\\\ 10 & =10\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the point $C$ does lie on the line.\n\nFinally, only points $A$ and $C$ lie on the line." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["9124fd28-3c96-58aa-a8b1-46f977a63903"] :db/ensure :question/validate} {:db/id "5a90128e-f77f-5ec3-9038-8600c7b3dcfd" :answer/id #uuid "5a90128e-f77f-5ec3-9038-8600c7b3dcfd" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$A$ and $C$ only" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "627354bc-e225-5d3c-9eda-85b7e4603569" :answer/id #uuid "627354bc-e225-5d3c-9eda-85b7e4603569" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$A$ only" :db/ensure :answer/validate} 