not lie on the line.\n\n- Substituting the point $C(2,4)$ results in true statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =2x \\\\ (4) & =2(2)+0 \\\\ 4 & =4\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the point $C$ does lie on the line.\n\nFinally, only points $A$ and $C$ lie on the line." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["ed72d909-9af6-5dcf-9647-d3ab941b4b50"] :db/ensure :question/validate} {:db/id "6965c31a-509c-5fad-b07e-299d62f499ff" :answer/id #uuid "6965c31a-509c-5fad-b07e-299d62f499ff" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$A$ and $C$ only" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "9a6fe6ee-5189-5bb5-9dc1-3ca7c751bd17" :answer/id #uuid "9a6fe6ee-5189-5bb5-9dc1-3ca7c751bd17" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$A$ only" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "ca1b1055-64cd-5ad9-a4f4-4ba68a08c842" :answer/id #uuid "ca1b1055-64cd-5ad9-a4f4-4ba68a08c842" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$B$ and $C$ only" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "49484dad-6a3e-55b6-a9bc-7f95d103cd98" :answer/id #uuid "49484dad-6a3e-55b6-a9bc-7f95d103cd98" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$B$ only" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "2517ee62-3508-5043-99a6-8cbff4a054bf" :answer/id #uuid "2517ee62-3508-5043-99a6-8cbff4a054bf" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$C$ only" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "030b1280-3f72-5e40-9687-4451485960c3" :answer-field/id #uuid "030b1280-3f72-5e40-9687-4451485960c3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/choices ["6965c31a-509c-5fad-b07e-299d62f499ff" "9a6fe6ee-5189-5bb5-9dc1-3ca7c751bd17" "ca1b1055-64cd-5ad9-a4f4-4ba68a08c842" "49484dad-6a3e-55b6-a9bc-7f95d103cd98" "2517ee62-3508-5043-99a6-8cbff4a054bf"] :answer-field/correct "6965c31a-509c-5fad-b07e-299d62f499ff" :db/ensure :answer-field/validate} {:db/id "277a1bc9-d733-576e-9af4-fb70571bb178" :question/id #uuid "277a1bc9-d733-576e-9af4-fb70571bb178" :question/problem "![](images/eb/eb6b3f51e0e61f72015505469f9fd6e6aa2d5e5b550825e4c761fc78f535ef59.png)\n\nIdentify the points that lie on the line $y=3x+2.$" :question/worked-solution "The plotted points correspond to the $xy$-pairs $A(-3,-7)$, $B(-1,1)$ and $C(1,5).$\n\nTo check whether a point lies on the line, we substitute the coordinates of the point into the equation and determine whether the resulting statement is true.\n\n- Substituting the point $A(-3,-7)$ results in a true statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =3x+2 \\\\ (-7) & =3(-3)+2 \\\\ -7 & =-7\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the point $A$ does lie on the line.\n\n- Substituting the point $B(-1,1)$ results in a false statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =3x+2 \\\\ (1) & =3(-1)+2 \\\\ 1 & =-1\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the point $B$ does not lie on the line.\n\n- Substituting the point $C(1,5)$ results in true statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =3x+2 \\\\ (5) & =3(1)+2 \\\\ 5 & =5\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the point $C$ does lie on the line.\n\nFinally, only points $A$ and $C$ lie on the line." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["030b1280-3f72-5e40-9687-4451485960c3"] :db/ensure :question/validate} {:db/id "2773d5bd-6a1e-5e0f-bdc4-1f27d274f0fc" :answer/id #uuid "2773d5bd-6a1e-5e0f-bdc4-1f27d274f0fc" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$A$ and $B$ only" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "4546836a-abb8-583d-8041-3599332cf4de" :answer/id #uuid "4546836a-abb8-583d-8041-3599332cf4de" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$A$ and $C$ only" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "961c8a45-200e-5ff7-841b-40c1e1f1d099" :answer/id #uuid "961c8a45-200e-5ff7-841b-40c1e1f1d099" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$A$ only" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "0b01faa9-1661-5d2c-8b15-89c1d529166b" :answer/id #uuid "0b01faa9-1661-5d2c-8b15-89c1d529166b" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$B$ only" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "86ff2819-d939-51c4-94f3-9732d4521a05" :answer/id #uuid "86ff2819-d939-51c4-94f3-9732d4521a05" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$C$ only" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "02799bef-6cfd-5d9e-bca3-3026a3cc6d51" :answer-field/id #uuid "02799bef-6cfd-5d9e-bca3-3026a3cc6d51" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/choices ["2773d5bd-6a1e-5e0f-bdc4-1f27d274f0fc" "4546836a-abb8-583d-8041-3599332cf4de" "961c8a45-200e-5ff7-841b-40c1e1f1d099" "0b01faa9-1661-5d2c-8b15-89c1d529166b" "86ff2819-d939-51c4-94f3-9732d4521a05"] :answer-field/correct "86ff2819-d939-51c4-94f3-9732d4521a05" :db/ensure :answer-field/validate} {:db/id "12a60b9c-85ce-50af-b45d-06caed36a198" :question/id #uuid "12a60b9c-85ce-50af-b45d-06caed36a198" :question/problem "![](images/3c/3cee718f18c9ef081b3e90a70d4db00ef0339d7d5f0b87423f7c5687709471a6.png)\n\nWhich of the given points lie on the line $y=-5x-2?$" :question/worked-solution "The plotted points correspond to the $xy$-pairs $A(-2,9),B(-1,4)$ and $C(1,-7).$\n\nTo check whether a point lies on the line, we substitute the coordinates of the point into the equation and determine whether the resulting statement is true.\n\n- Substituting the point $A(-2,9)$ results in a false statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =-5x-2 \\\\ (9) & =-5(-2)-2 \\\\ 9 & =8\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the point $A$ does *not* lie on the line.\n\n- Substituting the point $B(-1,4)$ results in a false statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =-5x-2 \\\\ (4) & =-5(-1)-2 \\\\ 4 & =3\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the point $B$ does not lie on the line.\n\n- Substituting the point $C(1,-7)$ results in a true statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =-5x-2 \\\\ (-7) & =-5(1)-2 \\\\ -7 & =-7\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the point $C$ does lie on the line.\n\nFinally, only point $C$ lies on the line." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["02799bef-6cfd-